 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 4.92,
   "text": "Before we look ten years ahead, I want to share a few ideas of my own.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.571,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 5.182,
   "e": 7.851,
   "text": "They are research directions, not results.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.669,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 8.417,
   "e": 10.737,
   "text": "Some of them may be wrong.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.32,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 10.957,
   "e": 14.202,
   "text": "But I think each one is worth someone's PhD.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.245,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 15.281,
   "e": 16.201,
   "text": "The first idea:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 0.92,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 16.789,
   "e": 23.029,
   "text": "rewire tiles, not synapses. Theorem three told us that random sparse graphs starve the GPU.",
   "dur": 6.24,
   "voiced": 369,
   "sim": 0.87,
   "f0": 119.257,
   "st": -0.108,
   "range_st": 4.253,
   "asr": 0.733,
   "attempts": 4,
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 23.612,
   "e": 26.828,
   "text": "But a tensor core does not see synapses.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.217,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 27.032,
   "e": 29.053,
   "text": "It sees small dense tiles.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.021,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 30.303,
   "e": 35.148,
   "text": "So what if structural plasticity worked at exactly that granularity,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.844,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 35.768,
   "e": 43.128,
   "text": "growing and pruning whole sixteen-by-sixteen blocks, the way RigL grows and prunes individual weights during training?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 7.36,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 43.625,
   "e": 46.615,
   "text": "The network still rewires its own topology,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.99,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 46.802,
   "e": 49.883,
   "text": "but every piece that survives stays dense.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.082,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 51.483,
   "e": 59.866,
   "text": "On my laptop, the same ninety percent sparsity ran five and a half times faster as sixteen-by-sixteen tiles than as scattered synapses,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 8.383,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 59.956,
   "e": 61.76,
   "text": "even with a naive implementation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.804,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 62.483,
   "e": 65.686,
   "text": "A real block-sparse kernel should close much more of the gap.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.203,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 66.675,
   "e": 74.715,
   "text": "The second idea: spectral homeostasis. Theorem one showed that local Hebbian learning collapses toward a single eigenvector.",
   "dur": 8.04,
   "voiced": 503,
   "sim": 0.863,
   "f0": 118.352,
   "st": -0.239,
   "range_st": 6.794,
   "asr": 0.914,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 74.935,
   "e": 79.067,
   "text": "Real neurons fight a similar runaway with homeostatic plasticity.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.132,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 79.291,
   "e": 83.691,
   "text": "What if the homeostatic target were the shape of the spectrum itself,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.4,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 84.021,
   "e": 90.55,
   "text": "so that every layer is gently pushed back whenever its effective rank starts to fall, using only statistics it can measure locally?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 6.529,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 90.956,
   "e": 93.409,
   "text": "The question I would most like answered is simple:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 2.453,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 93.978,
   "e": 99.716,
   "text": "can a purely local rule keep many modes alive, the way attention does?",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.738,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 100.667,
   "e": 101.617,
   "text": "The third idea:",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 0.951,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 102.228,
   "e": 104.075,
   "text": "let the network sleep.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.847,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 104.461,
   "e": 108.119,
   "text": "Brains separate fast learning from slow consolidation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.658,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 108.347,
   "e": 110.09,
   "text": "The hippocampus records the day,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.743,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 110.358,
   "e": 113.38,
   "text": "and sleep replays it into the cortex.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.022,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "s": 113.698,
   "e": 119.396,
   "text": "A language model could do the same. Fast weights and delta-rule memories, written during every conversation.",
   "dur": 5.698,
   "voiced": 367,
   "sim": 0.867,
   "f0": 117.383,
   "st": -0.382,
   "range_st": 5.424,
   "asr": 0.824,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "s": 119.893,
   "e": 125.515,
   "text": "Then, offline, replayed and distilled into the slow weights with ordinary backpropagation.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 5.622,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "s": 125.854,
   "e": 128.974,
   "text": "Plasticity at inference, stability in training.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.12,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "s": 129.233,
   "e": 135.191,
   "text": "Two timescales, and perhaps no catastrophic forgetting, if the replay is chosen well.",
   "dur": 5.957,
   "voiced": 358,
   "sim": 0.833,
   "f0": 116.592,
   "st": -0.499,
   "range_st": 4.196,
   "asr": 0.917,
   "attempts": 3,
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "i": 30,
   "s": 136.166,
   "e": 138.326,
   "text": "And the fourth: three-factor learning for credit.",
   "dur": 2.16,
   "voiced": 123,
   "sim": 0.661,
   "f0": 126.661,
   "st": 0.935,
   "range_st": 7.649,
   "asr": 0.875,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 31,
   "s": 139.576,
   "e": 147.096,
   "text": "A method called e-prop showed that eligibility traces stored at each synapse, combined with a single broadcast learning signal,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 7.52,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 32,
   "s": 147.583,
   "e": 151.753,
   "text": "can approximate backpropagation through time in spiking networks.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.17,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 33,
   "s": 152.053,
   "e": 153.966,
   "text": "Pair that with neuromorphic hardware,",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.913,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 34,
   "s": 154.086,
   "e": 158.628,
   "text": "and the variance explosion of Theorem three might finally be tamed.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 4.542,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 35,
   "s": 159.328,
   "e": 162.883,
   "text": "If any of these sparks something for you, run with it.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 3.555,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 36,
   "s": 163.334,
   "e": 165.306,
   "text": "That is how this field moves forward.",
   "sim": 0.0,
   "dur": 1.972,
   "asr": 0.0,
   "trusted": true,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  }
 ]
}